    "Full API spec": "include/Board.h: class Board { public: Board() noexcept; void clear() noexcept; std::uint16_t at(std::size_t r, std::size_t c) const noexcept; void set(std::size_t r, std::size_t c, std::uint16_t v) noexcept; void getRow(std::size_t r, std::array<std::uint16_t,4>& out) const noexcept; void setRow(std::size_t r, const std::array<std::uint16_t,4>& in) noexcept; void getCol(std::size_t c, std::array<std::uint16_t,4>& out) const noexcept; void setCol(std::size_t c, const std::array<std::uint16_t,4>& in) noexcept; bool isFull() const noexcept; bool hasEmpty() const noexcept; std::uint16_t maxTile() const noexcept; static std::size_t side() noexcept; }; Semantics: 4x4 grid with indices r,c in [0,3]. All size/index types use std::size_t (<cstddef>). Values are non-negative 16-bit (std::uint16_t) tiles; 0 means empty. Methods do not throw; callers must respect index preconditions (no bounds checking). include/Move.h: namespace Move { enum class Direction { Left, Right, Up, Down }; struct LineMoveResult { std::array<std::uint16_t,4> line; bool moved; std::uint32_t scoreGained; }; struct BoardMoveResult { bool moved; std::uint32_t scoreGained; }; LineMoveResult processLine(const std::array<std::uint16_t,4>& line) noexcept; BoardMoveResult applyMove(Board& board, Direction dir) noexcept; bool hasLegalMove(const Board& board) noexcept; } Semantics: processLine applies 2048 rules deterministically to a single 4-length line: 1) slide all non-zero values left, 2) merge adjacent equal tiles exactly once per source tile from left to right by doubling the left value and zeroing the right, accumulating scoreGained as the sum of merged values (post-merge value), 3) slide again; moved is true if resulting line differs from input. applyMove transforms the entire board for the given direction by extracting/processing rows or columns with the same slide-merge-slide rule and reapplying; returns total score gained and whether any cell changed. hasLegalMove returns true if any move would change the board (either an empty cell exists or any adjacent equal tiles exist in any direction). include/Spawner.h: class Spawner { public: bool spawn(Board& board) noexcept; void initialFill(Board& board) noexcept; }; Semantics: deterministic spawning, no randomness: spawn places a single tile with value 2 into the first empty cell in row-major order; returns true if a tile was spawned, false if the board is full. initialFill clears the board and places exactly two tiles of value 2 at the first two positions in row-major order (e.g., (0,0) and (0,1)). include/Game.h: enum class GameState { Ongoing, Won, Lost }; class Game { public: Game() noexcept; void reset() noexcept; bool move(Move::Direction dir) noexcept; const Board& board() const noexcept; std::uint32_t score() const noexcept; GameState state() const noexcept; private: /* Board board_; std::uint32_t score_; GameState state_; Spawner spawner_; */ }; Semantics: Game owns its Board and Spawner and tracks a 32-bit score. reset clears game state and uses Spawner::initialFill for deterministic start. move delegates to Move::applyMove; if no tiles moved, returns false and makes no changes. If tiles moved, increments score by scoreGained, calls Spawner::spawn once, then updates state: Won if Board::maxTile() >= 2048; Lost if not Won and Move::hasLegalMove(board) == false; otherwise Ongoing. All methods are noexcept and deterministic. Cross-file include/usage constraints: - All headers are self-contained and include their needed standard headers (<array>, <cstdint>, <cstddef>, <utility>, etc.). - Callers/tests include only headers under include/*.h; they must not include any src/*.cpp. - src/*.cpp implement exactly the interfaces declared in include/*.h. - Main is environment-dependent and may perform minimal printing, but core logic remains pure and testable.",
